course: dictionary
lesson: 6228
title: ml, the short way to write millilitres
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: ml is short for millilitre, a small unit for measuring liquid. You will see it on drink cans, medicine bottles and recipes. There are 1000 ml in 1 litre.
explain: «A litre is 1000 millilitres (ml).» To change litres to ml, multiply by 1000. To change ml to litres, divide by 1000. So 500 ml is half a litre.
explain: Shops use ml too. «To compare a small pack and a big pack fairly, work out the price for the same amount, called the unit price.» Always compare the same amount, not just the price on the label.
fact: ml is short for millilitre. In America the word is spelled milliliter.
fact: 1000 ml make 1 litre.
fact: A teaspoon holds about 5 ml, and a can of drink is about 330 ml.
fact: «A 330 ml can of regular cola has about 35 g of sugar.»
fact: The golden rule of a best buy is to compare the same amount. Four 250 ml juices at 50p make a litre for £2, but a 1 litre bottle for £1.60 is the better buy.
exercise: What does ml stand for? | a metre of rope | a minute | a kilogram | *millilitre
exercise: «After 4 glasses of 200 ml and a 150 ml cup, 2000 - 800 - 150 = 1050 ml are left.» How much is left? | *1050 ml | 950 ml | 1150 ml | 800 ml
exercise: How many ml are in 1 litre? | *1000 ml | 10 ml | 100 ml | 10000 ml
test: Which is the better buy for one litre: four 250 ml juices at 50p each, or a 1 litre bottle at £1.60? | They cost the same | Not enough information to decide | Four small juices, because there are four of them | *The 1 litre bottle
test: How many ml are in 2 litres? | 200 ml | 20 ml | *2000 ml | 20000 ml
exam: «A 330 ml can of drink is about how many litres?» | 3.3 litres | 330 litres | 33 litres | *0.33 litres
